menu "Siri Bridge Configuration"

    config WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            SSID for the ESP32 to join. Values land in sdkconfig, which is
            gitignored — set via `idf.py menuconfig`, never commit secrets to
            sdkconfig.defaults.

    config WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"
        default ""
        help
            WPA2 password. Leave empty for open networks.

    config MQTT_BROKER_URI
        string "MQTT broker URI"
        default "mqtt://homeassistant.local:1883"
        help
            URI of the Home Assistant MQTT broker. Use mqtts:// for TLS.

    config MQTT_USERNAME
        string "MQTT username"
        default ""

    config MQTT_PASSWORD
        string "MQTT password"
        default ""

    config DEBUG_TOUCH_FRAMES
        bool "Log raw touch frames to UART (diagnostic)"
        default n
        help
            When enabled, every touch notification (handle 0x003D) is logged
            to UART as hex with parsed x/y/pressure/finger fields. Intended
            for protocol diagnosis — for example, understanding how the
            circular touchpad encodes coordinates near its physical edges,
            where small swipes are misclassified.

            Adds significant log spam during touchpad use (~50 lines/sec).
            Disable for normal operation.

    config DEBUG_AUDIO_PCM_TCP
        bool "Stream decoded PCM over TCP (Phase 5.A.3 validation)"
        depends on VOICE_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            Diagnostic transport for the Phase 5.A.3 voice validation.
            On every Mic-button-driven audio session the bridge opens a
            TCP connection to AUDIO_PCM_TCP_HOST:AUDIO_PCM_TCP_PORT and
            streams the decoded 16 kHz mono int16le PCM frames as they
            come out of opus_decode(). On session end the socket closes.

            Listener (run on the host machine before pressing Mic):
                nc -l <PORT> | ffplay -f s16le -ar 16000 -ac 1 -

            Or save then play:
                nc -l <PORT> > capture.pcm
                ffplay -f s16le -ar 16000 -ac 1 capture.pcm

            Disable for normal operation. Phase 5.B replaces this with
            ESPHome's voice_assistant transport.

    config AUDIO_PCM_TCP_HOST
        string "TCP host for decoded PCM stream"
        depends on DEBUG_AUDIO_PCM_TCP
        default "192.168.1.100"
        help
            IPv4 address of the listener host. Override for your dev
            machine via menuconfig.

    config AUDIO_PCM_TCP_PORT
        int "TCP port for decoded PCM stream"
        depends on DEBUG_AUDIO_PCM_TCP
        default 8000
        range 1 65535

    config VOICE_ENABLED
        bool "Voice capture (Mic-button → Opus decode)"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, the bridge subscribes to the Siri Remote's
            audio characteristic (val handle 0x0035, CCCD 0x0036) and
            decodes the Opus frame stream during a Mic-button hold using
            the esphome/micro-opus library. Decoder runs on a dedicated
            task pinned to CPU1; OpusDecoder state lives in PSRAM
            (~50 KB). Per-frame RMS energy is logged to UART every ~1s
            for diagnostic visibility.

            With this disabled the bridge skips the audio CCCD subscribe
            (saving ~5 KB BLE buffer overhead) and doesn't allocate the
            decoder. Useful for users who don't want voice and want the
            smallest possible firmware.

            Phase 5.A.3 (TCP validation sink) and Phase 5.B (ESPHome
            voice_assistant integration) build on this; both require it
            to be enabled.

    config DEBUG_WAKE_PROBE
        bool "Wake-press loss probe (diagnostic)"
        default n
        help
            When enabled, the BLE connect path is instrumented with millisecond
            timestamps relative to BLE_GAP_EVENT_CONNECT (logged as `t=Xms`),
            and apply_remote_setup additionally subscribes to every
            unexplored notify-capable HID Report CCCD on the gen-3 remote
            (handles 0x0042 / 0x0046 / 0x004A / 0x0051 / 0x0054 / 0x0056 /
            0x0058). Combined with the existing notify-RX hex dump, this
            captures whether any unexplored handle carries the wake-button
            identity that's lost on cold-boot connects.

            Diagnostic only — leave disabled for normal operation.

    config BATTERY_LOW_THRESHOLD_PCT
        int "Battery low threshold (percent)"
        default 20
        range 0 100
        help
            When battery level is at or below this percentage, the published
            battery JSON includes "low": true. Set to 0 to always report
            "low": false (effectively disabling the alert field). HA can also
            do this kind of thresholding template-side; this knob just lets
            firmware-only setups have a sane low-battery flag.

    config PULSE_REPEAT_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Button pulse repeat interval (ms)"
        default 100
        range 0 60000
        help
            While a button is held, the bridge re-emits its event every this
            many milliseconds, carrying an incrementing "repeat" index and a
            measured "held_ms". Modelled on NEC IR repeat frames: there is no
            release event, and Home Assistant decides what holding means.

            This is a rate, not a policy. Do not treat it as a hold threshold
            — that judgment belongs in HA, which has the per-automation and
            per-context knowledge firmware does not.

            Bounded below by the 50 ms tick period; values between 1 and 49
            simply emit once per tick. Set to 0 to disable repeats entirely,
            leaving only the initial press (repeat 0).

    config BLE_SLAVE_LATENCY_DEFAULT
        int "BLE slave-latency default"
        default 400
        range 0 500
        help
            Initial BLE slave-latency value applied after the post-bond
            setup chain completes. The remote may deep-sleep between
            mandatory connection events for up to (latency * conn_itvl);
            higher values save battery, lower values reduce wake-press
            latency. Empirically 400 is the sweet spot — see Phase 3A.7
            notes in memory/project_gen3_protocol.md.

            Compile-time only. This used to be exposed as a runtime Number
            entity persisted in NVS; the pulse refactor removed the whole
            Number platform, so changing it now requires a reflash.

    config IDLE_DISCONNECT_MS
        int "Idle BLE disconnect threshold (ms)"
        default 0
        range 0 3600000
        help
            Idle window after which the bridge proactively terminates
            the BLE link.

            0 (default): always-connected mode. The link stays up forever
            using the remote's preferred low-power conn params (slave
            latency 80) so the remote still deep-sleeps between events.
            CR2032 lifetime ~10–15 months vs ~18–24 months disconnected,
            in exchange for 100% wake-press reliability.

            Non-zero (e.g. 60000): auto-disconnect on idle. Better battery,
            but Apple drops the press that wakes the remote if the bridge
            has been disconnected for >30s — the synthesized `pickup`
            event still fires as a generic wake signal. See README's
            "Always-connected mode" section.

endmenu
